Package: k9s
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: terminal UI to manage Kubernetes clusters
 K9s is a terminal UI to interact with your Kubernetes clusters. The aim of
 this project is to make it easier to navigate, observe and manage your
 applications in the wild.
 .
 K9s continually monitors Kubernetes for changes and offers shortcuts to
 interact with the resources it observes. It bundles a rich set of keyboard
 shortcuts to move around the cluster, inspect resource state, view and
 tail container logs, and run common administrative tasks without typing
 long kubectl commands.

# Note on the Go toolchain: k9s' go.mod requires Go >= 1.26.8, newer than
# trixie's golang-go. The build environment (see deb/Dockerfile) installs the
# pinned upstream Go; a distro golang-go with GOTOOLCHAIN=auto also works, as
# it fetches the required version itself. Dependencies are vendored
# (go mod vendor) so the package builds without network access.
